{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Quiet-window closeout and divergence disposition — 2026-08-26\n\nOutcome\n- The targeted rewrite published successfully. OLD_TIP=56236267c975e6d59156163678f0dc4e7771737b; rewritten epoch base=19708d1422a27edef2272afa6c7b882f8c188c8e.\n- Manifest digest=79687943ae1094051966679c31c36f5d0a0d938fb22b7000c88b63aab3edc165. Independently verified backup bundle SHA-256=37e6a0736ed631a852faae61fcda2d46162797c99d68d67bda770f8baa496963.\n- Writer freeze receipts showed the old tip stable at 23:32:36Z before Jira deletion and still stable at 23:38:56Z before publication. AWS/local/remote OID, deployed-epoch refusal, candidate replay, rollback/forward, and exact-lease publication checks passed.\n- Jira DELETE returned HTTP 204 for 997143, 997144, 997145, 997255, 997256, and 997293. Survivors 963510, 963511, 963512, 963788, 963789, and 964272 remained present; all non-target comment bytes were identical. The completed 12-record journal was replayed idempotently during this final check: it issued no new DELETE and matched the saved post-cleanup Jira observation exactly.\n- Whole-store replay and strict fsck passed during execution. Rollback reproduced OLD_TIP and forward replay reproduced the rewritten tip. The two production-runtime dry runs planned zero comment, label, or link operations with equal canonical plan digests.\n- All 1,520 removed path aliases remained absent after staged service restoration. Current origin/tickets=4ceb7b35127a84c54638e909ee4bd8594037a170 is descended from 19708d1422a27edef2272afa6c7b882f8c188c8e, and a fresh current-tree oracle again found 0 of 1,520 aliases.\n\nEvidence receipts\n- /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-comment-echo-window.YxHlh1/pre-jira-delete-freeze.json\n- pre-publication-freeze.json, jira-cleanup-verification.json, whole-store-replay.json, rollback-forward-receipt.json, rollback-replay.json, local-epoch-probe.json, dry-run-differential-receipt.json, dry-run-lifecycle-validation.json, and footprint-measurements.json in the same private off-repository directory.\n\nMeasured footprint\n- Tracked logical bytes: -254,356,888; tracked allocated bytes: -255,553,536; tracked files: -760.\n- This did not solve pack-history growth: the rehearsal candidate reachable pack was +354,184,985 bytes and whole-clone allocation was +98,484,224 bytes versus the old source. The checked-out payload reclaim is real, but history-retention remediation remains separate future work.\n\nService restoration\n- Reconcile Bridge run 33029396329 succeeded; heartbeat 33029925099 succeeded; dependency advisory 33030080673 succeeded; compaction dry run 33030247891 succeeded. All GitHub workflows are active.\n- The AWS MCP is healthy behind the intentional blue/green upstream on port 8093 with in_flight=0. The port difference is expected blue/green state, not a bug.\n- The review bot was recreated and is healthy. Its first backfill completed; Gerrit retains the durable review votes. The AWS autodeploy timer remains intentionally disabled because a secret refresh would remove the temporary overlap-drain setting.\n\nPreserved AWS divergence assessment\n- Forensic clone: /var/gerrit/site/retired-ticket-clones/reviewbot-tickets-divergent-376bc29e. It remains untouched and retained: HEAD=376bc29eadd42f9bb4335f4e365bf53119bb41d3; tracking ref=9ffd0f8ed06d458e54192cbc05d4ff391f49a58e; 399 commits ahead, comprising 312 merges and 87 non-merges. The diff has exactly 87 added paths and no modified or deleted paths; one untracked DONE_ENRICH remains preserved.\n- Event inventory: 65 ENQUEUE_ENRICH, 1 CLAIM_ENRICH, 5 CREATE, 7 REVIEW_RESULT, and 9 LINK events, totaling 220,198 bytes, plus the untracked DONE_ENRICH. There are no COMMENT, EDIT, STATUS, DELETE, or other user-ticket mutations and no hidden historical event paths.\n- All five CREATE events are code_review artifacts. src/rebar/review_bot/artifact_emit.py documents that emission occurs after the Gerrit vote and is best-effort because the vote is already durable; code_review is excluded from Jira reconciliation by src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/config.py. The nine links are only relates_to edges from those artifacts to existing implementation tickets.\n- Gerrit independently retains the exact review outcomes represented by the artifacts: change 2248 patch 1 has BLOCK then PASS and patch 2 PASS, now merged; change 2239 has the divergent patch 4 BLOCK twice and patch 5 BLOCK and remains active on patch 7; change 2247 patch 1 PASS is merged; change 2244 patch 2 BLOCK remains active on patch 3. Therefore losing the best-effort ticket sidecars does not lose the merge gate decision.\n- Of the 65 divergent enrichment enqueues, 50 already have an authoritative pending enqueue. The other 15 are present-fresh with done=true and pending=false; restoring them would only cause redundant enrichment. The single divergent claim lease had expired before commit and authoritative state already has a pending request. The untracked DONE_ENRICH predates the authoritative latest enqueue, so the reducer ignores it.\n\nDisposition: restore no divergent events. They are semantically redundant operational/enrichment records or best-effort code-review sidecars whose authoritative outcomes are durable in Gerrit. Restoring them would add stale or duplicate work without recovering user state. The divergence is safe to discard when the operator chooses, but the forensic clone has not been deleted, fetched, reset, or garbage-collected so the evidence remains available.\n\nFuture work deliberately remains open: apparent-sighted-cockatoo covers longer-horizon history policy and polite-antivirus-bedbug covers enrichment-growth remediation; neither acceptance scope was completed by this operation."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787798080405692001,"uuid":"95ac8e83-1993-4b62-8abe-be1084a18682"}